 17. From the aforesaid provision of Bill of lading Act, 1865, which is a prevailing statute in Bangladesh, it appears that upon endorsement and handover of the bill of lading to a person it gets the title to the cargo on board the vessel involved in the bill of lading along with the right to sue the defaulting parties as if the bill of lading has been issued in the name of the endorsee.&nbsp; 

